{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3LgDRzL1aV6sKTkHRm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AgR6Rc3N9w3URZMjT9MkQC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-064807__xe36ddc/work && cat > exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 06:48:07\",\n    \"source\": \"Cricket (over the top arcade style)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade sports (cricket), with a comedy story campaign\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow camera for lofted balls\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (engine unmodified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium 153\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's HD pixel Humanoids at 320x240 expanded; a TileMap ground with mown stripes, creases and rope; cricket kits, bats, stumps and crowd drawn in code\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's procedural rigs posed every step; the batter's swing uses the engine's slash move, timed to the contact\",\n    \"audio\": \"Chip-synth effects and three songs; Animalese-style formant gibberish voices for the commentary and the players; a noise crowd; all written in code, no audio files\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1: a parallel Super Over for 1 to 4 players, with the same six balls for every copy\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless suites with node test/run.mjs (physics, simulation, game flow, hub mock, bundle) and browser checks, including the AI Hub harness for 1, 2 and 4 players\",\n    \"research\": \"none (the engine's docs and the AI Hub protocol only)\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 for the browser checks\",\n    \"model\": \"claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"cost unknown; about 0.6M tokens (estimate from the session budget counter); session time about 40 minutes\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About a dozen issues were found, and all were fixed. The main ones: the rigs never animated, the bat and the pitch did not draw, the hub round played two innings, the idle timer ran late, and the touch-only gate was off.\",\n    \"Three were game-breaking for their feature: the hub round (two innings instead of one over), the rigs and bat (no animation or bat), and the idle timer (attract never started on time). All three are fixed, and none is known to be open.\",\n    \"The most helpful test was the headless match run to a result, which checks the scorecard against the ball records and the 15-second cap on play.\",\n    \"The least helpful was the toss timing check, which had to be rewritten after the flow changed; screenshots were slow to judge against the pixel detail.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The View system and the Humanoid rigs: custom Views with r.w projection gave a broadcast camera from the same primitives, and rigs draw cleanly inside actors.\",\n    \"Yes. An input preset without the default actions drew warnings, and drawing inside an actor uses its own local space, so absolute coordinates drew nothing. Both cost time.\",\n    \"The cricket simulation: ball physics and the predictor, timing grades, fielders and catches, running, the umpire, and the bat's drawing.\",\n    \"The hardest part was drawing in actor-local space and the font's missing symbols (the x sign, sigma, degrees and squared), which showed as question marks.\",\n    \"None. No engine file was changed; every change is in the game's own source.\",\n    \"A rig option for a two-handed bat grip, and a way to draw a world point inside an actor's callback.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The exact shape of the exit interview, and the explicit rules for the hub and for testing.\",\n    \"PLAN.md and TASK.md disagree on the folder name, the file name and the model suffix. TASK.md won, but reconciling them cost time. The plan is also much longer than one session.\",\n    \"Scope was the hardest part: five grounds, six teams, five chapters, around twenty specials and ten showreel segments do not fit one session. The demo was cut to three grounds, four teams, three chapters, five specials and three showreel segments.\",\n    \"A must-have list and an explicit scope budget, and a single set of names across the task and the plan.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Cricket Kerfuffle\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Over-the-top arcade cricket, with tea\",\n    \"description\": \"Smash sixes through the pub window, bowl flaming yorkers and take the village green from Lord Thrumpton across three outrageous grounds. Play up to four players on one screen, or Super Over rounds in AI Hub sessions.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Cricket\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or WASD aims · J ground shot · K loft · L defend · Space run · I special · controller: Cross, Square, Circle, Triangle\",\n    \"tags\": [\"sports\", \"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('exit-interview.json')); print('parses; keys', list(d))\" && mkdir -p CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-064807/engine && cat > CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-064807/engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2)\n\nNone. The game's engine files are the handoff package's, unmodified (`engine/my-3d2dge.js`, `engine/modules/`, `engine/kits/`).\n\nEverything the plan asked of the engine was built in the game instead:\n\n- The cricket bat is drawn by the game (`src/30-present.js`, `G.batInto`), in the rig's own draw space.\n- Cricket gear (pads, helmets, gloves) is approximated with the rig's existing hats, hair and kit colours.\n- The formant voice synthesizer runs on the engine's audio context (`src/44-audio.js`), with no change to the audio module.\n- The button-symbol setting is the game's own (`buttons` in `src/00-head.js`), not the engine's glyph option.\n- The pause items are added to the engine's `menu.items` array at start (`src/99-start.js`); in an AI Hub session the array is emptied (`src/50-hub.js`).\nEOF\nls -la /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-064807__xe36ddc/work/ | head -12","description":"Write the exit interview and the engine-changes note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":561926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1116},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c23f3159-3d46-4aa8-a3bf-9445ed47c313","uuid":"72e73752-0a2a-48b9-a3e8-f24b3894d975","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:25:05.907Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3Lfqcn5bCzDHdr8nju","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AgR6Rc3N9w3URZMjT9MkQC":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-064807__xe36ddc/work && cat > exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 06:48:07\",\n    \"source\": \"Cricket (over the top arcade style)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade sports (cricket), with a comedy story campaign\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow camera for lofted balls\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (engine unmodified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium 153\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's HD pixel Humanoids at 320x240 expanded; 