{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3eGUgcJGXCjiVJRTWf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cricket Kerfuffle is built. The single-file game and `exit-interview.json` are in the folder root, and `node test/run.mjs` passes all 149 checks. The demo is much smaller than PLAN.md describes, though, so read the cut list below before treating this as complete.\n\n**Files**\n- `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-064807.html` (about 1.4 MB, from `file://`, no network requests). The AI Hub client is the first script in `<head>`, byte-identical to the vendored copy.\n- `exit-interview.json` (TASK.md's exact shape, parses, every field filled).\n- The dev folder is `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-064807/` (`src/`, `tools/build.mjs`, `test/run.mjs`, `vendor/aihub/`).\n\n**Reading choices**\n- TASK.md wins over PLAN.md on names, the suffix, and the file location. \"Root\" is the folder that holds STAGE.md.\n- The title \"Cricket Kerfuffle\" is the one PLAN.md recorded from its RNG pick. I did not re-run the 50-title brainstorm.\n\n**What's in the demo**\n- Batting with timing grades (PERFECT, GOOD, EARLY, LATE, MISS), shot resolution from the button, stick and ball length, edges, and running with run-outs.\n- Bowling with three deliveries, a release meter, a marker, and field presets (R1 cycles them).\n- Fielding with catches, a catch ring for human fielders, and throws to either end.\n- Umpiring for bowled, caught, LBW (with one review per innings), wide and no-ball.\n- Hype, ON FIRE, two specials, items, stadium targets, and chaos events. The tide, gulls, peacock and cow have real effects; bells is caption-only.\n- The Kerfuffle Method rain delay, a Super Over on a tie, and Nets (free practice and the Six Machine).\n- The Showdown, versus for two players, and the story map.\n- Commentary as captions with gibberish voices, plus a synthesized crowd and music.\n- PlayStation glyphs by default and an Xbox option; prompts follow the last device; a touch-only gate.\n- Attract after 10 seconds idle; any input exits.\n- Dev mode from the pause menu, with live sliders and reset to defaults.\n- AI Hub parallel Super Over. The harness passes for 1, 2 and 4 players (4 on a slow, lossy link).\n\n**Verification**\n- `node test/run.mjs` runs 149 checks across six suites: physics, simulation, game flow, hub mock, bundle, and browser (Chromium, plus the AI Hub harness for 1, 2 and 4 players).\n- CPU-versus-CPU matches finish on every ground with no ball in play over 15 seconds, and each scorecard adds up.\n- Balance is about 7 to 8.5 runs an over. Wickets are about 0.3 an over, below the plan's 0.6 target; the sliders are the place to tune it.\n\n**Cut from PLAN.md**\n- 3 grounds (not 5), 4 teams with generated squads (not 6 with hand-made stars), 3 chapters (not 5), and 1-on-1 versus only.\n- No left-handed batters, no night or fog ground, no dive, no charge, no Owl-Eye or third-umpire screen, and no highlights reel.\n- 5 specials (not about 20), 3 items (not 7), and 3 attract segments (not 10).\n- The bowling-machine-only Showdown score has no initials table.\n- The replay setting was removed, since there is no replay system behind it.\n- No engine files were changed. The bat, the formant voice and the button-symbol setting are built in the game, and `engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md` says so.\n\n**Usage:** cost is unknown. About 0.6M tokens (estimate from the budget counter). About 40 minutes of session time.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 06:48:07\n- Source: Cricket (over the top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and perspective: arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story; broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow camera\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (unmodified), AI Hub client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium 153\n- Art direction: the engine's HD pixel Humanoids; a TileMap ground with creases and rope; cricket kits, bats, stumps and crowd drawn in code\n- Animation: the engine's rigs posed every step; the batter's swing uses the engine's slash move\n- Audio: chip-synth effects and three songs; formant gibberish voices; noise crowd; all in code\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel Super Over for 1 to 4 players\n- Testing: `node test/run.mjs` (headless, bundle, browser, AI Hub harness)\n- Research: none beyond the engine docs and the hub protocol\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 for browser checks\n- Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: cost unknown; about 0.6M tokens (estimate); about 40 minutes\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found: about a dozen, all fixed. The main ones: the rigs never animated, the bat and pitch did not draw, the hub round played two innings, the idle timer ran late, the touch gate was off, and the input preset dropped the menu actions.\n- Critical (game-breaking for their feature): the hub round, the rigs and bat, and the idle timer. All three are fixed, and none is known to be open.\n- Most helpful: the headless match runs to a result, with the 15-second cap and the scorecard check.\n- Least helpful: the toss timing checks, which had to be rewritten after the flow changed.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the View system and the rig draw, with `r.w` projection for every point.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: an input preset without the defaults warns, and actor drawing uses local space, so absolute coordinates draw nothing. Each cost time once.\n- Built ourselves: ball physics and the predictor, timing, fielders, running, the umpire, and the bat.\n- Hardest: drawing inside actors, and the font's missing symbols (×, σ, °, ²), which showed as question marks.\n- Changed in the engine: none.\n- One thing to change: a two-handed bat grip rig option, and world-point drawing inside an actor.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the exact exit-interview shape, and the explicit hub and testing rules.\n- Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md disagree on names. TASK.md won, but reconciling them cost time.\n- Hardest: the plan is far bigger than one session, so the scope had to be cut.\n- Change: a must-have list, a scope budget, and one set of names."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2214,"cache_read_input_tokens":578605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2214},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c23f3159-3d46-4aa8-a3bf-9445ed47c313","uuid":"ed685faf-be29-4ec7-99c7-515a42783735","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:29:03.812Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3eG1eqn3ZxMqzE2n4Y"}
