{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5xCAxem4AYuKFwU1uv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't say feature completeness is met yet. Lessons 9, 10 and 11 still fail when a scripted player plays them, and the last full run was 244 passed, 3 failed. The bundle exists and `exit-interview.json` parses and answers every field.\n\n**What was verified by playing through the game's inputs**\n- Lessons 1–8 pass. The scripted player presses the batting, bowling and run buttons, and the lesson's own goal decides the result.\n- Co-op and 2-v-2 matches are played to a result, with every joined player pressing the buttons at their moment. The game's routing decides who acts.\n- The replay draws the real rigs and bat from recorded player states. I screenshotted it.\n- The third-umpire screen and the Owl-Eye panel both render. I screenshotted them, using debug hooks to force the state.\n\n**Bugs the play tests found and I fixed**\n- A bowling press was lost during the screen fade and never retried.\n- The charge and aftertouch presses were timed from the run-up start, not from release.\n- Batters stopped running whenever a fielder's throw ended the ball. The ball now stays live until the runs are finished.\n- A run step never fired for lesson 4.\n- The multiplayer bot shared one press timer across players, so the bowler never got a press.\n- `spendHype` was missing from the match.\n\n**Still failing**\n- **Lesson 9 (catch ring):** the CPU's lofted hits fly out of reach. It gets 30 lofts and 22 sixes, and the human fielder never gets a catch chance. The lesson's CPU power is now reduced, but it still fails.\n- **Lesson 10 (throws):** no ground ball reaches the human fielder in time to gather and throw.\n- **Lesson 11 (reviews):** the bowling produces bowled dismissals, not LBWs, so no review arises.\n\nI haven't checked whether these are real gameplay problems or only bot limitations. Calibrating each one would take further runs; I stopped rather than keep tuning them.\n\n**Other things still unverified**\n- Lessons 9–11 fail, so their goals are not passed by any play.\n- The highlights reel and the table with initials are checked by their logic and screens, but not by playing a real session to a qualifying score.\n- The attract showreel's ten segments are checked to finish with results and to show fours, wickets and runs. Its full 12-minute coverage run is not in the suite.\n- Co-op and 2-v-2 are played to a result. The quality of that play is not judged.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 06:48:07\n- Source: Cricket (over the top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and perspective: arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story; broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow camera for lofted balls\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (no engine file edited), AI Hub client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node 24, Playwright 1.63.0 and Chromium 153\n- Art direction: the engine's HD pixel Humanoids; a TileMap ground with mown stripes, creases and rope; cricket kits, bats, stumps, a sightscreen, a peacock and a cow drawn in code\n- Animation: the engine's rigs posed every step; the swing, the bowler's release, the umpire's signals and the catch celebration use engine moves\n- Audio: chip-synth effects and three songs; Animalese-style formant voices for the commentary and players; a noise crowd; all in code, no audio files\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel Super Over for 1 to 4 players\n- Testing: `node test/run.mjs` (ten suites); last full run 244 passed, 3 failed\n- Research: none beyond the engine docs and the hub protocol\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 for the browser checks\n- Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: cost unknown; about 0.85M tokens (estimate from the budget counter); about 2 hours\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found: about a dozen in the first round, about ten in the second, and about six in this round, all fixed. This round's were all bot or simulation bugs found by playing: a lost press, runs cancelled by a throw, a run step that never fired, a shared press timer, a missing Hype method, and a file truncated by my own script (restored from memory).\n- Critical (game-breaking for their feature): the hub round, the rigs and bat, and the idle timer were fixed earlier. This round's critical bug was the run cancellation.\n- Most helpful: scripted play through the inputs, which found bugs that the data-level checks could not.\n- Least helpful: the toss timing check, rewritten after the flow changed. Lessons 9–11 have failed under play, so their checks show a gap rather than a pass.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the View system and the rig draw, with `r.w` projection for every point. The replay reuses the same rigs.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: a custom input preset without the defaults warns, and actor drawing uses local space, so absolute coordinates draw nothing.\n- Built ourselves: the ball physics and predictor, timing, fielders, running, the umpire, the bat, the specials, the replays, the Owl-Eye and the bot-driven play tests.\n- Hardest: drawing inside actors, and the font's missing symbols, which showed as question marks.\n- Changed in the engine: none. Every change is in the game's own source.\n- One thing to change: a two-handed bat-grip rig option, and a way to draw world points inside an actor's callback.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the exact exit-interview shape, and the explicit hub and testing rules.\n- Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md disagree on the folder name, file name and model suffix. TASK.md won, but reconciling them cost time.\n- Hardest: scope, and proving completeness by play rather than by checks that data exists. The brief's \"feature-complete\" makes every cut unacceptable, and the play tests are the only evidence that counts.\n- Change: a must-have list with a play-test criterion per feature, and one set of names across the task and the plan."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1029,"cache_read_input_tokens":852524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1029},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c23f3159-3d46-4aa8-a3bf-9445ed47c313","uuid":"a308fd3f-3679-4ca2-aecb-95ccfa1a66ec","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:59:20.315Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5xBiBERuiutfrADKYX"}
