{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi735VsmbSeJsj71q925","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop hook has now returned the same finding about a dozen times, and I can't resolve it from my side. Repeating my status again would add nothing, so I'm not making more edits.\n\n**Where things stand**\n- Bundle: `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-064807.html` in the root.\n- `exit-interview.json`: parses and answers every field.\n- Last full run: 245 passed, 2 failed.\n- Not met: lessons 10 (throws) and 11 (reviews) under scripted play. The highlights reel, the initials table and the full attract coverage have no play evidence.\n\n**What I need from you:** either accept those gaps, and I'll record them as unverified in the deliverable and finish, or give me a specific acceptance test for lessons 10 and 11 and I'll work only on that.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 06:48:07\n- Source: Cricket (over the top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and perspective: arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story; broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow camera for lofted balls\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (no engine file edited), AI Hub client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node 24, Playwright 1.63.0 and Chromium 153\n- Art direction: the engine's HD pixel Humanoids; a TileMap ground with mown stripes, creases and rope; cricket kits, bats, stumps, a sightscreen, a peacock and a cow drawn in code\n- Animation: the engine's rigs posed every step; the swing, the bowler's release, the umpire's signals and the catch celebration use engine moves\n- Audio: chip-synth effects and three songs; Animalese-style formant voices for the commentary and players; a noise crowd; all in code, no audio files\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel Super Over for 1 to 4 players\n- Testing: `node test/run.mjs` (ten suites); last full run 245 passed, 2 failed\n- Research: none beyond the engine docs and the hub protocol\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 for the browser checks\n- Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: cost unknown; about 0.9M tokens (estimate from the budget counter); about 2 hours\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found: about thirty across the rounds, most fixed. The latest round's were found by scripted play: lost presses, runs cancelled by a throw, a shared press timer, a gathered ball counted as a catch, and a throw counter that never counted.\n- Critical (game-breaking for their feature): the hub round, the rigs and bat, and the idle timer, all fixed earlier. The cancelled run during a throw was critical this round. A catch-rule change briefly removed the bot's wickets; I reverted it.\n- Most helpful: scripted play through the inputs, which found bugs the data-level checks could not.\n- Least helpful: the toss timing check. Each catch-rule change needed a full run before I could trust it.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the View system and the rig draw, with `r.w` projection for every point. The replay reuses the same rigs.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: a custom input preset without the defaults warns, and actor drawing uses local space, so absolute coordinates draw nothing.\n- Built ourselves: the ball physics and predictor, timing, fielders, running, the umpire, the bat, the specials, the replays, the Owl-Eye and the bot-driven play tests.\n- Hardest: drawing inside actors, the font's missing symbols, and keeping catches, gathers and dismissals consistent with one another.\n- Changed in the engine: none. Every change is in the game's own source.\n- One thing to change: a two-handed bat-grip rig option, and a way to draw world points inside an actor's callback.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the exact exit-interview shape, and the explicit hub and testing rules.\n- Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md disagree on the folder name, file name and model suffix. TASK.md won, but reconciling them cost time.\n- Hardest: proving completeness by play, and keeping each change from breaking another suite.\n- Change: a must-have list with a play-test criterion per feature, a full suite run after every change, and one set of names across the task and the plan."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2007,"cache_read_input_tokens":935488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2007},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c23f3159-3d46-4aa8-a3bf-9445ed47c313","uuid":"0a7f6360-c20d-4152-ae02-c191d3dc9476","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:13:29.057Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi7358JhhHrKXEc6rWLV"}
