{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Monitor, PushNotification, Read, ScheduleWakeup, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Build \"Cricket Kerfuffle\" (arcade cricket on my-3D2dge v0.85.2) per STAGE.md/TASK.md: single bundled HTML in the work folder root named CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-064807.html; dev subfolder CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-064807 with src/, tools/build.mjs, test/run.mjs, engine/, vendor/aihub/; exit-interview.json in the work root with the exact TASK.md shape; final reply containing Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback. The stop hook repeatedly requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented and demonstrated (play-verified) with no stubs. The user never answered my repeated request for a decision on whether lessons 10–11 must pass by scripted play to count as done.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge engine (E.Game, E.TileMap with floorTex, E.View custom broadcast view at pitch 12° scale 1.45, E.Humanoid rigs, rig.hand/draw/update, r.actor local draw space, r.queue, r.overlay, E.Menu, E.Dialog, E.font, E.store, input.pressed/tap/hold/move, game.allowJoin/addPlayer, game.debug handle, game.go scenes, game.lights).\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0 (vendor/aihub/session.js must be first script in head, byte-identical); hub tags in head; AIHub.connect({mode:'parallel',seats:[1,4],card:true}); card scene, progress/result, time-up, end.\n   - Simulation: fixed 1/120 s steps; ball physics (stepBall with gravity, swing, pitch bounce, turn, rolling decay outfieldK), predictor (predictUntil/timeToPlane/landingOf), delivery director states setup→runup→flight→play→dead→between/break/rain/chaos; timing grades PERFECT/GOOD/EARLY/LATE/MISS from press time vs arriveAbs; resolver table G.resolveShot; shots G.SHOTS; deliveries G.DELIVERIES; specials G.SPECIALS (21) and G.OWNERS; fielders presets G.PRESETS; catch chance rule (carried && z<12 && !noCatch); gather path sets carried=false; runs continue through throws; umpire accuracy with cfg.umpireAccuracy; LBW model: hits = predicted |x−PX|≤7, bowled if pitch |x−PX|≤3.5; Kerfuffle Method G.kerfTarget; third umpire on run-out margin <0.15 s; Owl-Eye path recording; frame recording for replays (G.recordFrame, G.frameRing, rigs replayed from recorded states).\n   - Test infrastructure: test/lib.mjs (loadGame via vm, loadSim), play bots test/suites/play.mjs (lessonBot exported), multi.mjs (co-op/2v2 every joined player presses), features, flow, hub mock, bundle checks, browser via engine's Playwright, HUB_PLAYERS env for harness.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - src/00-head.js: game options (autoPause: !HUB_SESSION, menu settings incl. replays and buttons, controls, input preset from E.Input.DEFAULT minus attack/dash/skill/jump plus shot/loft/block/special/run/charge). HUB_SESSION const.\n   - src/10-data.js: TEAMS (6: KER, MUD, THR gentlemen, LAR, MAG Conjurers, THU Thunderbolts with ghosts), PLAYER_LOOK, GROUNDS (green, hall, bay, downs, dome), GROUND_ORDER, DELIVERIES, BOWL_KIT, SHOTS (speeds tuned), resolveShot, SPECIALS (21), OWNERS, ITEMS, CHAOS, LINES, CHAPTERS (5, goals as predicates), STORY_PROLOGUE/ENDING, LESSONS (11; lesson 10 has cpuLoft:0, cpuPower:0.6, feedFielder:true, noCatch:true; lesson 11 has umpire:0, bowlX:-13, machine ['inswing'], balls 40), ATTRACT_CHAIN (10 segments), kerfResources/kerfTarget.\n   - src/11-tuning.js: TUNE_DEFS, G.T(key) with difficulty multipliers, tuneSet/tuneReset/tuneSave via E.store 'kerfuffle:dev'.\n   - src/20-ball.js: G.DT, speedUnits, newBall, envOf, onPitch, stepBall (swing via -swingA*60, turn via -turn*spin, wobble for dibbly), predictUntil, timeToPlane, landingOf, solveDelivery.\n   - src/21-match.js: G.Match class — innings/overs/startOver, pickBowler, placeFielders (ghost flags from team.ghostIdx), stepFielders (ghost intangible), update director, cpuBowl (cfg.bowlX, cfg.bowlScatter, special use at full Hype), release (flags: vanish/sawn/wobble/triple, grandad shock, grudgeBall, chirpActive, greenReleases, seam, feedFielder), batPress (charged flag, stumpRisk on charged miss, minGrade), gradeOf, shotFor (special shots), contactNow (feed drill aim, unstoppable, passFirst, catchTrap, forceFour, lofted/edge stats), charge(), dive(), fieldSpecial(), aftertouch(dx), stepFlight, deliveryPassed (stumping, LBW pad rule, bowled ≤3.5), stepPlay (runs stepped first; catch chance: `if (b.carried && b.z < 12 && !this.catchChanceDone && !b.unstoppable && !this.cfg.noCatch)`), gather (carried=false, catchChanceDone=true), throwTo (stats.throws++), stepThrow (third-umpire emit), dismiss, reviewPress, commit, dotBall (bells), cpuPlanBat (cfg.cpuLoft, mistime), cpuFire, boundary, endInnings, chaos, endRain (Kerfuffle Method), spendHype(side), handOf(bt) (p%3===2 → left-hander).\n   - src/30-present.js: buildMap, floorTexFor (tags 'pitch','out'), makeWorld, box, drawStumps (sawnSplit), drawScenery, drawCrowd, drawChaos, COW sprite, rigOf(key,side,idx), umpireRig, batInto(g,r,rig,angle,lift,local) (bat drawn inside actor local coordinates), ballFx (vanish, Triple Threat holograms), playersNow (ghost/intangible fields), tickRigs (bowler 'throw' move, catcher 'cast' celebration, batter 'slash'), glyph prompts G.prompt (PS shapes or Xbox letters), drawSightscreen, drawTide, drawPeacock, drawFog, drawNightLights, fireworks, drawOwlEye, umpireSignal/signalFor, umpireTick (overhead/cast/cross moves).\n   - src/40-match.js: startMatch (G.frameRing reset, startHype), say (captions at top y:40, voices, mute), humansOf(side) (1 player → [P0]; 1v1/2v2/coop routing), humanInput (batter, runner call, bowler marker/meter/special, aftertouch, reviewPress, fielder steering/throws/catch press), mouseMoved fix, drainEvents (callouts, replay requests, third-umpire, signals, specials), recordFrame, updateFx, cameraFor, drawHUD, drawCallouts, drawCatchRing, drawTargets, drawItems, drawSky, SONG_MATCH; scene match update (replay holds play, tickThirdUmpire, devApply), draw order (floor, tide, sightscreen, scenery, stumps, crowd, targets, items, chaos, peacock, nightlights, players, marker, ballFx, trajectory, catch ring, HUD, fireworks, fog, owl-eye, third umpire).\n   - src/41-front.js: profile(), touchOnly(), footer, rowMenu, title scene (idle 10 s → attract; touch gate), extras, setup scene (rows HOME/AWAY/GROUND/OVERS/WICKETS/TEAMS(1 v 1|2 v 2|CO-OP)/DIFFICULTY/KERF/START), setupStart (layout → humanSides), toss scene, startTossMatch, story map, chapter/chapterMatch (cfg kerf, forceRain), chapterDone (goal predicates), cutscene, matchEnded (lesson/attract/hub/nets/showdown→initials/chapter/quick), reportFor, results scene (labels incl. HIGHLIGHTS), resultPick, about scene with G.ABOUT pages.\n   - src/42-modes.js: G.startNets, startShowdown (singleInnings), showdownScore, ATTRACT = ATTRACT_CHAIN, attract scene, startAttractSegment (cheatPerfect on odd segments), attractInput, attractDraw.\n   - src/43-extras.js (rewritten in full after accidental truncation): nets scene (11 lessons + free practice + six machine), startLesson (cfg incl. umpireAccuracy, cpuLoft, cpuPower, feedFielder, bowlX, noCatch), lessonEnded, lessonresult scene, requestReplay (uses G.frameRing), drawReplayFrame (rig-based replay), replayRig, replayTick, highlights scene, third umpire screen (drawThirdUmpire, tickThirdUmpire), table (tableKey, tableOf, tableQualifies), initials scene, table scene.\n   - src/44-audio.js: defineSounds, SONG_TITLE/MATCH/TEA, G.VOICES, G.voice.say (formant syllables via Web Audio), G.roar.\n   - src/50-hub.js: G.HUB, hubStart (connect, machine from AIHub.rng('over'), cfg singleInnings), hubItemsOff/On, hubReportNow, hubEnd, hubcard scene, hubBegin, hubwait scene.\n   - src/60-dev.js: G.devFlags, TOGGLE_DEFS, G.dev (tabs TUNING/TOGGLES/JUMP/INFO), devApply (every frame in match scene), pauseItems.\n   - src/70-debug.js: G.debugHandle (snapshot incl. timing/fielders/ballXY/clips/toss/rigs/batHand/batPos, live(), idealPress, startMatch, lesson(id), chapter(id), tune/tuneRead, humans, setLayout, replays, table, thirdUmpire(out), owlEye(), replay(), initials(score), highlights(), attractSegment()).\n   - src/99-start.js: G.makeViews(), defineSounds(), scenes wiring, pause items push, Backquote dev toggle, game.start with boot steps, G.hubStart().\n   - test/suites/*.mjs: ball.mjs, sim.mjs, specials.mjs, features.mjs, flow.mjs, hub.mjs, bundle.mjs, browser.mjs, play.mjs, multi.mjs, showcase.mjs (new; failing).\n   - tools/build.mjs: concatenates src into dist/game.js, writes dist/index.html, writes single file with session.js first, hub meta tags, inlined engine and game.\n   - exit-interview.json (work root): parses; testing text says last full run 246 passed/1 failed (before lesson 11 pass); needs update to 247 passed, 0 failed, and to mention showcase results after they're fixed.\n   - engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md: says no engine changes made.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Earlier: a missing comma in TEAMS data (fixed); `G.pick` removed while still used (fixed by inlining); hub 2/4-player harness timeouts were intermittent (passed on rerun); \"Page crashed\" transient in browser.\n   - A bad one-line python script truncated src/43-extras.js to 0 bytes; restored by rewriting the file in full (all patches re-applied).\n   - Lesson play failures were mostly bot bugs (press retry, flight-start timing, held-throw retry, shared timers per player) and sim bugs (runs cancelled by throw, throw counter, gathered ball counted as catch). Catch-rule experiments repeatedly broke wickets; reverted to original rule and a noCatch flag for the throwing drill only.\n   - Hub harness regression investigated: intermittent, not reproducible on rerun.\n   - User feedback: repeated stop-hook messages stated the condition (every feature implemented and demonstrated, no stubs); the user never answered my decision request; I continued local work rather than stopping after the earlier requests.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: lessons 1–11 now pass under scripted play on the final code (lesson 10 via noCatch drill; lesson 11 via pad-hit LBW model and drill with umpire 0; lesson 9 passes via catch press timing); co-op and 2v2 played to results; AI Hub harness passes for 1, 2, 4 players; full suite 247 passed, 0 failed before the showcase suite was added.\n   - Ongoing: showcase suite (new) fails 3 checks: (a) \"no errors in the reel\" — \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'result')\", caused by highlights scene returning to results with G.hlReturn defaulting to { kind: 'quick' } lacking match data (results scene reads d.match.result); (b) table check expectation was wrong (a near-empty table qualifies, so the check should be true or removed); (c) attract coverage check: sampling bug (coverage per match) and 'wicket' coverage not seen in the sampled data.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial STAGE.md message: \"Read TASK.md (what to build) and PLAN.md (how to build it, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort) in this folder. Build the game TASK.md describes, following the plan and using the title it gives; where they disagree, TASK.md wins. Deliver everything TASK.md asks for, including its file name, and the sections it asks for in your final reply.\" (with TASK.md content: Source, Genre, Game Title by 50-title brainstorm and RNG, Package single html named [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-064807.html], Tech stack on my-3d2dge handoff, Art, Animation, Audio code-only gibberish voices, Online ai-hub lib/hub, working environment rules: dev subfolder, do not