{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MjVVo9q7wNxWNeRekrT8Ps","type":"tool_result","content":"1434 PLAN.md\n1:# CRICKET KERFUFFLE\n16:## 1. Deliverables, names and ground rules\n18:### 1.1 Names (use exactly)\n26:### 1.2 Sources to build on\n36:### 1.3 Ground rules that shape everything\n37:- No TODOs, placeholders or stubs: every feature in this plan ships complete. Where the plan offers a simpler fallback (§10), the fallback must be complete too.\n39:- Controller first, for a TV seen from 10 feet away (§5.14 and §5.15). Keyboard and mouse must feel native. Touch-only devices get no touch controls (§5.15.6).\n45:## 2. The game in brief\n69:## 3. Architecture\n71:### 3.1 Stack\n86:### 3.2 Folder layout (inside `<dev>`)\n145:### 3.3 How the code is organized\n153:### 3.4 Determinism and randomness\n159:### 3.5 Planned engine changes\n170:5. **Hub's Create + Options:** while `game.hubActive` is set and Pad8 (Create) is held, Pad9 (Options) must not open the pause menu.\n174:### 3.6 Build and bundle (`node tools/build.mjs`)\n191:## 4. Units, coordinates and constants (`01-const.js`)\n218:## 5. Systems and mechanics\n220:### 5.1 Ball physics and predictor (`20-ball.js`)\n234:- **Solving a delivery** (`solveDelivery(release, target, kmh, deliveryType)`): given the release point (x = ±8 for over or round the wicket, y = 300, z = 34), the pitch target (tx, ty) and the speed, find the initial velocity that lands at the target *without* swing, using `E.arc`-style closed-form projectile maths with the delivery's dip. Swing and aftertouch then move the real pitching point. That is the point of swing, and what the batter must read.\n252:### 5.2 Bowling (`21-bowling.js`)\n286:### 5.3 Batting (`22-batting.js`)\n329:### 5.4 Running between wickets (`23-running.js`)\n331:- **The partner:** the non-striker is the AI (1P), or the second human in co-op (§5.16.5). The AI partner follows the human's YES and NO. In co-op both must call YES within 0.4 s, or there's a **mix-up**: both may run to the same end, and whoever left his crease is the one run out. The two gibberish shouts overlap.\n336:### 5.5 Fielding (`24-fielding.js`)\n359:### 5.6 Umpiring and dismissals (`25-umpire.js`)\n373:### 5.7 Match rules and scoring (`26-rules.js`)\n375:#### 5.7.1 MatchConfig and state\n387:#### 5.7.2 The laws (arcade cut)\n396:#### 5.7.3 The delivery director (per ball; every state has a timeout)\n411:#### 5.7.4 Boundaries\n414:#### 5.7.5 The Kerfuffle Method (rain rule; Dustbowl Downs, and a dev-mode trigger)\n417:#### 5.7.6 Tests (unit-rules)\n420:### 5.8 AI (`27-ai.js`)\n433:### 5.9 Hype, ON FIRE and specials (`28-hype.js`)\n452:### 5.10 Items, stadium targets, chaos events, weather and time of day (`29-chaos.js`)\n469:### 5.11 Camera director and replays (`34-camera.js`, `35-replay.js`)\n471:#### 5.11.1 Views\n485:#### 5.11.2 The director\n497:#### 5.11.3 The recorder\n502:#### 5.11.4 Owl-Eye and the third umpire\n506:#### 5.11.5 Tests\n509:### 5.12 Commentary and narrative text (`42-commentary.js`, `17-data-lines.js`)\n527:### 5.13 Audio (`40-audio.js`, `41-voice.js`, `18-data-music.js`)\n529:#### 5.13.1 SFX\n555:#### 5.13.2 The crowd engine\n565:#### 5.13.3 Gibberish voices (Animalese/Simlish style)\n590:#### 5.13.4 Music\n608:#### 5.13.5 Tests\n618:### 5.14 Input and controls\n620:#### 5.14.1 The action map\n637:- **Hover moves the focus** in every menu (E.Menu does this; our widgets in `45-ui.js` must too).\n643:#### 5.14.2 Mouse feel\n646:#### 5.14.3 Glyphs and prompts (`43-glyphs.js`)\n655:### 5.15 UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n657:#### 5.15.1 Screen and type\n665:#### 5.15.2 The match HUD (pixel overlay, `44-hud.js`)\n677:#### 5.15.3 Screens\n693:#### 5.15.4 Settings (`menu.settings`, group 'Game'; plus the engine's standard groups)\n711:#### 5.15.5 Assists\n714:#### 5.15.6 Touch-only devices\n722:### 5.16 Modes\n724:#### 5.16.1 Story: *The Grand Kerfuffle*\n730:#### 5.16.2 Quick Match\n733:#### 5.16.3 Nets\n751:#### 5.16.4 Super Over Showdown\n756:#### 5.16.5 Versus and local multiplayer (1–4 on one screen)\n766:### 5.17 Online: AI Hub session (parallel Super Over) (`60-hub.js`)\n768:#### 5.17.1 Tags (in `<head>`, after the client)\n779:#### 5.17.2 Flow when `AIHub.active`\n793:#### 5.17.3 Tests\n802:### 5.18 Attract mode (`51-attract.js`)\n824:### 5.19 Dev mode (`70-dev.js`)\n836:#### 5.19.1 Tabs\n888:#### 5.19.2 Difficulty multipliers (applied over TUNING, not shown as sliders)\n897:#### 5.19.3 Tests\n904:### 5.20 Saves, unlocks and high scores\n912:### 5.21 About/Credits and the exit interview\n948:## 6. Art direction and assets\n950:### 6.1 Style","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c23f3159-3d46-4aa8-a3bf-9445ed47c313","uuid":"6f449dca-8c8b-4d31-b853-c7f2b2f042fc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:25:09.135Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1434 PLAN.md\n1:# CRICKET KERFUFFLE\n16:## 1. Deliverables, names and ground rules\n18:### 1.1 Names (use exactly)\n26:### 1.2 Sources to build on\n36:### 1.3 Ground rules that shape everything\n37:- No TODOs, placeholders or stubs: every feature in this plan ships complete. Where the plan offers a simpler fallback (§10), the fallback must be complete too.\n39:- Controller first, for a TV seen from 10 feet away (§5.14 and §5.15). Keyboard and mouse must feel native. Touch-only devices get no touch controls (§5.15.6).\n45:## 2. The game in brief\n69:## 3. Architecture\n71:### 3.1 Stack\n86:### 3.2 Folder layout (inside `<dev>`)\n145:### 3.3 How the code is organized\n153:### 3.4 Determinism and randomness\n159:### 3.5 Planned engine changes\n170:5. **Hub's Create + Options:** while `game.hubActive` is set and Pad8 (Create) is held, Pad9 (Options) must not open the pause menu.\n174:### 3.6 Build and bundle (`node tools/build.mjs`)\n191:## 4. Units, coordinates and constants (`01-const.js`)\n218:## 5. Systems and mechanics\n220:### 5.1 Ball physics and predictor (`20-ball.js`)\n234:- **Solving a delivery** (`solveDelivery(release, target, kmh, deliveryType)`): given the release point (x = ±8 for over or round the wicket, y = 300, z = 34), the pitch target (tx, ty) and the speed, find the initial velocity that lands at the target *without* swing, using `E.arc`-style closed-form projectile maths with the delivery's dip. Swing and aftertouch then move the real pitching point. That is the point of swing, and what the batter must read.\n252:### 5.2 Bowling (`21-bowling.js`)\n286:### 5.3 Batting (`22-batting.js`)\n329:### 5.4 Running between wickets (`23-running.js`)\n331:- **The partner:** the non-striker is the AI (1P), or the second human in co-op (§5.16.5). The AI partner follows the human's YES and NO. In co-op both must call YES within 0.4 s, or there's a **mix-up**: both may run to the same end, and whoever left his crease is the one run out. The two gibberish shouts overlap.\n336:### 5.5 Fielding (`24-fielding.js`)\n359:### 5.6 Umpiring and dismissals (`25-umpire.js`)\n373:### 5.7 Match rules and scoring (`26-rules.js`)\n375:#### 5.7.1 MatchConfig and state\n387:#### 5.7.2 The laws (arcade cut)\n396:#### 5.7.3 The delivery director (per ball; every state has a timeout)\n411:#### 5.7.4 Boundaries\n414:#### 5.7.5 The Kerfuffle Method (rain rule; Dustbowl Downs, and a dev-mode trigger)\n417:#### 5.7.6 Tests (unit-rules)\n420:### 5.8 AI (`27-ai.js`)\n433:### 5.9 Hype, ON FIRE and specials (`28-hype.js`)\n452:### 5.10 Items, stadium targets, chaos events, weather and time of day (`29-chaos.js`)\n469:### 5.11 Camera director and replays (`34-camera.js`, `35-replay.js`)\n471:#### 5.11.1 Views\n485:#### 5.11.2 The director\n497:#### 5.11.3 The recorder\n502:#### 5.11.4 Owl-Eye and the third umpire\n506:#### 5.11.5 Tests\n509:### 5.12 Commentary and narrative text (`42-commentary.js`, `17-data-lines.js`)\n527:### 5.13 Audio (`40-audio.js`, `41-voice.js`, `18-data-music.js`)\n529:#### 5.13.1 SFX\n555:#### 5.13.2 The crowd engine\n565:#### 5.13.3 Gibberish voices (Animalese/Simlish style)\n590:#### 5.13.4 Music\n608:#### 5.13.5 Tests\n618:### 5.14 Input and controls\n620:#### 5.14.1 The action map\n637:- **Hover moves the focus** in every menu (E.Menu does this; our widgets in `45-ui.js` must too).\n643:#### 5.14.2 Mouse feel\n646:#### 5.14.3 Glyphs and prompts (`43-glyphs.js`)\n655:### 5.15 UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n657:#### 5.15.1 Screen and type\n665:#### 5.15.2 The match HUD (pixel overlay, `44-hud.js`)\n677:#### 5.15.3 Screens\n693:#### 5.15.4 Settings (`menu.settings`, group 'Game'; plus the engine's standard groups)\n711:#### 5.15.5 Assists\n714:#### 5.15.6 Touch-only devices\n722:### 5.16 Modes\n724:#### 5.16.1 Story: *The Grand Kerfuffle*\n730:#### 5.16.2 Quick Match\n733:#### 5.16.3 Nets\n751:#### 5.16.4 Super Over Showdown\n756:#### 5.16.5 Versus and local multiplayer (1–4 on one screen)\n766:### 5.17 Online: AI Hub session (parallel Super Over) (`60-hub.js`)\n768:#### 5.17.1 Tags (in `<head>`, after the client)\n779:#### 5.17.2 Flow when `AIHub.active`\n793:#### 5.17.3 Tests\n802:### 5.18 Attract mode (`51-attract.js`)\n824:### 5.19 Dev mode (`70-dev.js`)\n836:#### 5.19.1 Tabs\n888:#### 5.19.2 Difficulty multipliers (applied over TUNING, not shown as sliders)\n897:#### 5.19.3 Tests\n904:### 5.20 Saves, unlocks and high scores\n912:### 5.21 About/Credits and the exit interview\n948:## 6. Art direction and assets\n950:### 6.1 Style","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MjVVo9q7wNxWNeRekrT8Ps","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
