{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi8Vdv7FD7GHf439NKRS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build is updated and the full suite passes: 272 passed, 0 failed, across 12 suites. The stop condition is still not met. Some TASK.md and PLAN.md items are unfinished, and I'm reporting them below rather than calling the demo complete.\n\n## What I checked against the brief\n\nI went through TASK.md and the plan's feature sections, then checked each against the source and the suites. Here is what this pass found and changed:\n\n- **Running (Manual or Auto):** missing. Added the setting. Auto calls the run once the ball is on the ground. Brief suite: Manual runs nothing, Auto runs without a button press.\n- **Continue and New Game:** missing. STORY now offers Continue or New Game when a saved story exists. New Game asks before it clears chapters and stars, and keeps unlocks and stats. Checked.\n- **Quick Match unlocks:** missing. Quick Match offers only unlocked opponents, and a win unlocks the other side. I chose to start with the first two sides open, because the plan doesn't say. Checked by recording a win; the match-end path itself isn't played through.\n- **Career stats:** missing. Total sixes and fastest ball are now saved to the profile. Checked on a played match.\n- **About page:** the in-game text still said \"219 checks in eight suites.\" Corrected to 272 in twelve suites.\n- **Audio:** the bundle has no audio file references. Checked.\n- **Already present and checked by existing suites:** attract, dev mode and sliders, touch gate, pause menu, co-op and 2v2, the AI Hub harness, the highlights reel, the initials table, and the showreel.\n\nI also added the brief suite, which holds these checks, and the showcase fixes from the last pass. `exit-interview.json` now lists the suites, the 272 checks, and the open gaps.\n\n## Still open\n\n- **Reviews under the normal rules:** not demonstrated. In 20 ordinary showreel segments there were 12 wickets and zero reviews. Reviews only happen when a human presses the review button. Lesson 11 shows the review through a drill. This needs a design decision about how often umpires refer decisions, or a scripted human who reviews in an ordinary match.\n- **Full story playthrough:** no bot plays New Game through the five chapters to the ending. The plan asks for one, and TASK.md lists a scripted whole-game playthrough among the tests. This is the largest item left.\n- **Lessons 10 and 11:** they pass only with drill settings, as before.\n- **Not covered by any suite:** the Xbox glyph switch and mouse aiming.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:48:07\n- **Source:** Cricket (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and perspective:** arcade sports with a comedy story; broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (engine unmodified), AI Hub client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio\n- **Art, animation, audio:** engine HD pixel rigs with cricket kits drawn in code; procedural swing; chip-synth songs and effects, formant gibberish voices, crowd noise; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub parallel Super Over, 1 to 4 players\n- **Testing:** twelve suites, one command, 272 checks passing\n- **Research:** none beyond the engine and AI Hub docs\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 for browser checks\n- **Model:** claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost unknown; about 0.8M tokens (estimate from the session budget counter); session time about 2.5 hours\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about a dozen in the first round and about ten in the second, all fixed. This pass added four more that were real gaps: Running, Continue, the unlocks and stats, and the stale About count.\n- **Critical:** the hub round playing two innings, the rigs and bat not drawing, and the idle timer running late. All fixed.\n- **Most helpful:** the headless match run to a result, and the brief suite, which found items the earlier suites missed.\n- **Least helpful:** the toss timing check, which needed rewriting after the flow changed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the View system and rig drawing; custom broadcast views came from the engine's own primitives.\n- **Stuck or guessed:** an input preset without the defaults warns, and drawing inside an actor uses local coordinates.\n- **Built ourselves:** the ball physics and predictor, timing, fielders, running, the umpire, the bat, and the profile and unlock rules. The engine's store is enough for the profile.\n- **Hardest:** broadcast-style drawing inside actors, and world points inside actor callbacks.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** a rig option for a two-handed grip.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the exact exit-interview shape and the explicit testing rules.\n- **Confusing:** TASK.md and PLAN.md disagree on names, and TASK.md's feature list is short while the plan's is long. The plan's items that TASK.md doesn't name are easy to miss.\n- **Hardest:** the plan is bigger than one session. The full story playthrough and normal-rule reviews are the two items I didn't finish.\n- **Change:** list the must-have features once, with a pass check for each, so the enumeration isn't left to the builder.\n\nI did not commit anything. The next step I'd take is the full-campaign bot, then reviews in an ordinary match."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1880,"cache_read_input_tokens":142313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1880},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c23f3159-3d46-4a